<ServiceLayout title="Disc Injury" description="Chiropractic treatment for disc injuries, herniated discs, and bulging discs at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH." schemaType="MedicalCondition">
<p>The discs between your vertebrae act as cushions — absorbing shock and allowing your spine to move freely. When a disc is damaged through injury, wear, or misalignment, it can bulge or herniate, pressing on nearby nerves and causing significant pain.</p>
<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />
<h2>Types of disc problems</h2>
<p>Disc problems range from bulging discs (where the disc extends beyond its normal boundary) to herniated discs (where the inner material pushes through the outer wall) to degenerative disc disease (where discs gradually wear down over time). Each type can cause pain, numbness, and reduced mobility.</p>
<h2>Chiropractic approach</h2>
<p>Our chiropractors use gentle, specific techniques to improve spinal alignment and reduce pressure on affected discs. This can help relieve pain, promote healing, and restore function. We take a conservative approach, working to help you avoid more invasive treatments whenever possible.</p>
</ServiceLayout>
